  "name": "Homies — Chatwoot handback",
  "description": null,
  "active": true,
  "isArchived": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "hb-sticky",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Hand quiet conversations back to the bot\n\nAn agent takes a conversation (assign / `bot-off` label) and the bot goes\nquiet on it. If the thread then sits silent for **15 minutes**, this hands it\nback -- unassigns and strips the label -- so the resident's next message gets\nanswered instead of waiting on someone who left.\n\n15 min was chosen 21 Aug over the proposed 2: `last_activity_at` only moves on\nmessages, so a short limit steals threads from agents who are typing or on the\nphone. Resolved conversations are never touched.\n\nReads the first page of open conversations (25). Fine at today's volume;\npaginate before the pilot if handovers exceed that.\n\nThere is deliberately NO permanent opt-out yet: every handover expires. If a\nthread must stay human forever, that is a feature request, not a label.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hb-tick",
      "name": "Every minute",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "minutes",
              "minutesInterval": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hb-fetch",
      "name": "Fetch open conversations",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        220,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://chat.srv1879140.hstgr.cloud/api/v1/accounts/2/conversations",
        "sendQuery": true,
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "status",
              "value": "open"
            }
          ]
        },
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 15000
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "1qfgfvxwZ4MsUBBh",
          "name": "Chatwoot admin (api_access_token)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hb-filter",
      "name": "Quiet for 15 minutes?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        440,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "\n// Which handed-over conversations have gone quiet?\n//\n// The bot is off on a conversation that is assigned or labelled bot-off (the\n// same two signals the WhatsApp workflow's gate reads -- keep them in step).\n// 15 minutes of silence hands it back. last_activity_at moves on every\n// message either way, so an agent mid-conversation is never interrupted;\n// an agent who took a thread and left is overridden a quarter hour later.\nconst LIMIT = 15 * 60;\nconst now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);\nconst out = [];\nfor (const c of ($input.first().json.data?.payload ?? [])) {\n  // A bot-inbox conversation is assigned to the AGENT BOT by Chatwoot itself;\n  // that is not a handover and must not be \"handed back\" every 15 minutes.\n  const a = c.meta?.assignee;\n  const t = c.meta?.assignee_type;\n  const assignee = a && (t ? t === 'User' : !a.outgoing_url) ? a : null;\n  const labels = c.labels ?? [];\n  if (!assignee && !labels.includes('bot-off')) continue;   // bot already on\n  const quiet = now - (c.last_activity_at ?? now);\n  if (quiet < LIMIT) continue;                              // still being worked\n  out.push({ json: {\n    conv_id: c.id,\n    keep_labels: labels.filter(l => l !== 'bot-off'),\n    quiet_minutes: Math.floor(quiet / 60),\n  }});\n}\nreturn out;\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hb-unassign",
      "name": "Unassign",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        660,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "=https://chat.srv1879140.hstgr.cloud/api/v1/accounts/2/conversations/{{ $json.conv_id }}/assignments",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ assignee_id: null }) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 15000
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "1qfgfvxwZ4MsUBBh",
          "name": "Chatwoot admin (api_access_token)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hb-strip",
      "name": "Strip the bot-off label",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        880,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "=https://chat.srv1879140.hstgr.cloud/api/v1/accounts/2/conversations/{{ $('Quiet for 15 minutes?').item.json.conv_id }}/labels",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ labels: $('Quiet for 15 minutes?').item.json.keep_labels }) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 15000
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "1qfgfvxwZ4MsUBBh",
          "name": "Chatwoot admin (api_access_token)"
        }
      }
    }
